["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"service-sdk","stream_identity":"01a0d3f5-e04a-747a-a30b-acde601bf68b","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"story","fields":{"body":"## Outcome\n\nA generated Identity HTTP service package remains directly executable while downstream consumers can compile only its client/library surface.\n\n## Context\n\nGenerated packages currently make `service-host` unconditional. A client consumer therefore resolves the service's SQLite adapter and can collide with its own persistence stack even though it never runs the generated binary.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Identity HTTP packages expose the standalone host as a default feature and mark host-only dependencies optional.\n- The generated binary explicitly requires that host feature.\n- Consumers can disable default features and use the generated typed client without resolving the host adapter.\n- Generation tests assert the feature and binary contract; generated standalone builds retain their current behavior.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nSplitting the generated library into separately published crates or changing service HTTP semantics.\n\n## Scope\n\nService Builder Rust package generation, tests, documentation, and release notes.\n","document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"ent-5230b2afb7dd919d26b487cd1ea6c75a","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/generated-client-host-separation","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":5,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"## Outcome\n\nA generated Identity HTTP service package remains directly executable while downstream consumers can compile only its client/library surface.\n\n## Context\n\nGenerated packages currently make `service-host` unconditional. A client consumer therefore resolves the service's SQLite adapter and can collide with its own persistence stack even though it never runs the generated binary.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Identity HTTP packages expose the standalone host as a default feature and mark host-only dependencies optional.\n- The generated binary explicitly requires that host feature.\n- Consumers can disable default features and use the generated typed client without resolving the host adapter.\n- Generation tests assert the feature and binary contract; generated standalone builds retain their current behavior.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\nSplitting the generated library into separately published crates or changing service HTTP semantics.\n\n## Scope\n\nService Builder Rust package generation, tests, documentation, and release notes.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:builder-runtime"},{"serves":"vision:composable-services"}],"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":"CHANGELOG.md"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Cargo.lock"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Cargo.toml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"README.md"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/service-builder"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"Let consumers use an SDK-generated client without linking the service process host or persistence adapter.","title":"Separate generated clients from standalone hosts"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"},"relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:builder-runtime"},{"serves":"vision:composable-services"}],"scope":[{"confidence":"cited","path":"CHANGELOG.md"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Cargo.lock"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"Cargo.toml"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"README.md"},{"confidence":"cited","path":"crates/service-builder"}],"summary":"Let consumers use an SDK-generated client without linking the service process host or persistence adapter.","title":"Separate generated clients from standalone hosts"},"id":"ent-5230b2afb7dd919d26b487cd1ea6c75a","lifecycle_state":"implemented","revision":5,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["story","ent-5230b2afb7dd919d26b487cd1ea6c75a"]}]